    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9eqrm6o",
      "content": "Chhattisgarh follows the parliamentary system of governance as prescribed by the Constitution of India. The state has a unicameral legislature (Vidhan Sabha). The Governor is the constitutional head of the state, while the Chief Minister and the Council of Ministers exercise executive power."
    },
