    {
      "id": "ttkgukp",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3.2 Administrative Divisions"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0yncs7x",
      "content": "The state is divided into 5 divisions, 33 districts, sub-divisions, tehsils, blocks, and village panchayats. The district collector (IAS officer) heads each district and is responsible for land administration, law and order, and implementation of government schemes."
    },
    {
      "id": "3q9xmqd",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3.3 Panchayati Raj System"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "79uveh2",
      "content": "Chhattisgarh has a three-tier Panchayati Raj system:"
    },
    {
      "id": "25qcupu",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Gram Panchayat (Village level)",
        "Janpad Panchayat (Block level)",
        "Zila Panchayat (District level)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "y3gdd7g",
      "content": "The Panchayats Extension to Scheduled Areas (PESA) Act, 1996 is implemented in the 5th Schedule areas of Chhattisgarh, giving tribal panchayats special powers over natural resources, land, and traditional customs."
    },
    {
      "id": "lbn5ywi",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3.4 State Police Structure (Important for SI Exam)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nk0y4w9",
      "content": "The Chhattisgarh Police is headed by the Director General of Police (DGP). The state is divided into police ranges, each headed by an Inspector General of Police (IGP). Districts are headed by Superintendent of Police (SP). The hierarchy from bottom to top is: Constable → Head Constable → Assistant Sub-Inspector (ASI) → Sub-Inspector (SI) → Inspector → Deputy Superintendent of Police (DSP) → Additional Superintendent of Police (ASP) → Superintendent of Police (SP) → Senior Superintendent of Police (SSP) → Deputy Inspector General (DIG) → Inspector General (IG) → Additional Director General (ADG) → Director General of Police (DGP)."
    },
